course: dictionary
lesson: 14501
title: Pedigree: one word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Pedigree has more than one meaning, so context tells you which one to use. «The farmer showed the judge the pedigree of his prize bull.» Here pedigree means the list of the bull's parents and ancestors, which proves it is a pure breed.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Dogs, horses and cattle at shows point to the animal meaning. «The club has a pedigree of winning cups» has no animals, so pedigree means a past record that shows something is good.
explain: To check, swap in an easier word, such as record, history or background. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: Pedigree (noun) means the list of an animal's parents, grandparents and earlier ancestors.
fact: Pedigree (adjective) describes an animal from parents of the same breed, with records, as in «a pedigree dog».
fact: Pedigree can also mean a person's family background, or the past record of something, such as «the team's winning pedigree».
fact: In science, a pedigree chart shows how features like eye colour pass through a family.
exercise: «The puppy's pedigree lists its parents and grandparents.» What is a pedigree here? | A kind of lead | A type of dog food | A record of an animal's parents and ancestors | *A dog show prize with ribbons
exercise: «The football club has a pedigree of winning cups.» What does pedigree mean? | *A past record that shows the club is good | A new kit for the team | A list of the players' birthdays | A map of the stadium
exercise: What does «pedigree» tell us about «a pedigree dog»? | It has a long tail | *It comes from parents of the same breed, with records | It is very fast | It lives indoors all the time
test: «The horse's pedigree goes back five generations.» What does the pedigree show? | *Its parents and ancestors, back through the family | Its best race times only | Where it was born | Its colour and size
test: «Ella's family pedigree includes three generations of teachers.» What does pedigree mean here? | A school timetable | A dog show record | A list of favourite books | *Family background
exam: A pedigree chart in a science lesson shows what? | A map of the school grounds | *How features such as eye colour pass through a family | The price of a farm animal | How fast a dog can run
